\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Song information\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The OpenNeuro page says each participant completed \'93Twenty music-listening sessions are named as ses-txx\'94 and that \'93ses-t01 corresponds to song_id = t01\'94; each session is a different song. It also states each music session lasts 130 seconds: \'935 seconds before onset, 120 seconds of playback and 5 seconds after offset.\'94[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nemar.org/dataset/on008701"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 nemar}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://openneuro.org/search/modality/eeg"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 openneuro}}]\
However, I found 
\f0\b no source listing the 20 song titles, artists, audio files, or a public t01\'96t30 mapping
\f1\b0 . The IEEE DataPort description says songs are grouped into five affective classes and that labels are in 
\f2\fs26 labels.xlsx
\f1\fs24 , but it does not identify the songs. Song-title/audio availability: 
